#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:3
msgid "Fixed-Point Arithmetic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:5
msgid "Standards and Goals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:7
msgid ""
"`stdfix.h` is specified in [ISO/IEC TR 18037:2008](https://www.iso.org/"
"standard/51126.html), C extensions to support embedded processors ([publicly "
"available specification](https://standards.iso.org/ittf/"
"PubliclyAvailableStandards/c051126_ISO_IEC_TR_18037_2008.zip))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:10
msgid ""
"Our goal is to implement a complete set of math functions for fixed-point "
"types, most of which are not included in ISO/IEC TR 18037:2008.  Our math "
"functions for fixed-point types are modelled after the C99/C23 math "
"functions for floating-point types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:15
msgid "Source Location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:17
msgid ""
"The main source for fixed-point functions is located at [libc/src/stdfix]"
"(https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/libc/src/stdfix), with "
"internal support utilities under [libc/src/\\_\\_support/fixed_point]"
"(https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/libc/src/__support/"
"fixed_point)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:22
msgid "Implementation Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:24
msgid ""
"Per-precision function, macro, and type status tables: {doc}`../headers/"
"stdfix`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:26
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:28
msgid ""
"Building LLVM-libc with fixed-point arithmetic support requires a compiler "
"that supports the native fixed-point types `_Fract` and `_Accum` in C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:30
msgid ""
"Consuming the generated `stdfix.h` header requires compiler support for "
"`_Fract` and `_Accum` in C or C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:32
msgid ""
"Compiler support is checked at the top of [libc/include/llvm-libc-macros/"
"stdfix-macros.h](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/libc/include/"
"llvm-libc-macros/stdfix-macros.h)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:35
msgid "Predefined Macros"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:37
msgid ""
"`LIBC_COMPILER_HAS_FIXED_POINT` indicates whether the compiler supports "
"fixed-point types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:39
msgid ""
"Predefined precision and range macros from ISO/IEC TR 18037:2008 section "
"7.18a.3 are defined in [libc/include/llvm-libc-macros/stdfix-macros.h]"
"(https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/libc/include/llvm-libc-"
"macros/stdfix-macros.h) using the default `typical desktop processor` "
"configuration from Annex A.3 when compiler predefined macros are absent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:45
msgid "Formatted I/O"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:47
msgid ""
"ISO/IEC TR 18037:2008 section 7.18a.6.7 also specifies fixed-point "
"conversion specifiers (`r`, `R`, `k`, `K`) for the `<stdio.h>` `fprintf` and "
"`fscanf` families (`LIBC_CONF_PRINTF_DISABLE_FIXED_POINT` controls `printf` "
"support)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:51
msgid "Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../math/stdfix.md:53
msgid ""
"This support is currently a work in progress; its headers, macros, and ABI "
"are still unstable and may change."
msgstr ""
